{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["YHWH came from Sinai — He revealed Himself to Israel and gave them His Torah." "And shone — illumination." "From Seir — and Paran. How? 'that He came from among myriads of holy ones' — from all four sides of Mount Sinai the illumination and the angels came by way of Seir and Paran until He came to Sinai, and from His right hand He gave them [the Law] from amidst the fire, which was speaking to Israel, as it is written: ״השמע עם קול אלהים מדבר מתוך האש כמונו ויחי״. And so we find in Psalms: ״רכב אלהים רבותים אלפי שנאן ה׳ בם סיני בקדש״. And in Habakkuk: ״אלוה מתמן יבא וקדוש מהר פארן סלה כסה שמים הודו״. And in Deborah it is written: ״ה׳ בצאתך משעיר בצעדך משדה אדום״." "He shone forth from Mount Paran — He illuminated from Mount Paran."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:03.645647610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}